<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        A course is a set of reading sections followed by a short multiple-choice quiz.
        Open it from <a href="/training">My Training</a>.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Reading the sections">
        <ol>
            <li>Open the course from My Training.</li>
            <li>Read each section all the way through. The <strong>Next</strong> button unlocks
                once you've scrolled to the bottom of the section.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Previous</strong> to go back to a section you've already read.</li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Answering the quiz">
        <ol>
            <li>Choose one answer for each question, using <strong>Next</strong> to move through them.</li>
            <li>On the last question, press <strong>Done</strong> to submit your answers.</li>
            <li>Your score is shown straight away. You need to reach the course's pass mark to complete it.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            If you don't pass, each question is marked with a tick or a cross. Change your answers
            and press <strong>Retry</strong>. There's no limit on attempts, and every attempt is
            recorded.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
        If a course says it doesn't have a quiz yet, it can't be completed. Let your manager know so
        they can add the questions.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
